subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctrlshiftOFF/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctrlshiftOFF","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Investigacao-Filosofica/giflabs/commits/c3e8aeeb406813108c765a05b3e4b0deb5673a9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-05T01:55:02Z","email":"donteatyourprettypet@gmail.com","name":"OFF"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-05T01:55:02Z","email":"donteatyourprettypet@gmail.com","name":"OFF"},"message":"Proxy Strapi API and update blog fetches\n\nAdd a Next.js proxy for Strapi and switch blog fetches to use it. next.config.mjs now exposes STRAPI_URL and a rewrite from /api/strapi/* to the Strapi instance to avoid CORS in the browser. The blog pages (src/app/blog/page.tsx and src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx) introduce STRAPI_BASE which uses the client-side /api/strapi proxy and falls back to the direct NEXT_PUBLIC_STRAPI_URL on the server, and all relevant fetch calls were updated to use STRAPI_BASE. Update strapi/config/server.ts to set the public URL from PUBLIC_URL and enable proxy (koa: true) so Strapi trusts X-Forwarded-* headers when running behind proxies (eg. Railway). These changes enable same-origin API calls from the browser and better proxy handling in production.","tree":{"sha":"082adcfb5c52172badbf8739d84eb0b73b23dab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Investigacao-Filosofica/giflabs/git/trees/082adcfb5c52172badbf8739d84eb0b73b23dab1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Investigacao-Filosofica/giflabs/git/commits/c3e8aeeb406813108c765a05b3e4b0deb5673a9a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87695763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctrlshiftOFF/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctrlshiftOFF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ct