://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commit/ac6e4582534c5a2049ec4a4133cfda53bae9cea6","node_id":"C_kwDOPPKKzNoAKGFjNmU0NTgyNTM0YzVhMjA0OWVjNGE0MTMzY2ZkYTUzYmFlOWNlYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commit/5f0a68530883f70996608319cd5b601d1ccc1392","sha":"5f0a68530883f70996608319cd5b601d1ccc1392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commits/5f0a68530883f70996608319cd5b601d1ccc1392"}],"sha":"ac6e4582534c5a2049ec4a4133cfda53bae9cea6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commits/ac6e4582534c5a2049ec4a4133cfda53bae9cea6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114657827?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/YakupHadutoglu","id":114657827,"login":"YakupHadutoglu","node_id":"U_kgDOBtWKIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commits/5f0a68530883f70996608319cd5b601d1ccc1392/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-12T17:26:59Z","email":"yakuphad2004@gmail.com","name":"YakupHadutoglu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-12T17:26:59Z","email":"yakuphad2004@gmail.com","name":"YakupHadutoglu"},"message":"feat(analyzer): complete overhaul of the analysis module for architecture, performance, and security\n\nPurpose:\n- Address issues where the existing analysis module was slow on large-scale projects, produced incomplete reports, and was vulnerable to certain security risks.\n- Provide more accurate code quality metrics, support multiple naming conventions, and generate more detailed, bilingual (TR/EN) reports.\n\nMain Changes:\n1. Naming and Reporting:\n   - Added support for kebabCase, PascalCase, camelCase, snake_case, UPPER_SNAKE.\n   - Standardized errors[] array for structured error storage.\n   - Added TR/EN bilingual reporting with improved type safety.\n\n2. Complexity Analysis:\n   - New algorithm with 9 weighted factors and logarithmic normalization.\n   - Detection of deep folder structures, empty folders, and overpopulated directories.\n\n3. Architecture and Dependency Analysis:\n   - Detection of monolithic, microservices, serverless, and hybrid architectures.\n   - Extraction of package dependencies and security vulnerability (CVE) scanning.\n   - Framework detection (Node.js, Django, Spring, etc.).\n\n4. Performance and Large File Support:\n   - Stream-based extraction and mmap optimization for archives >10GB.\n   - Parallel processing and LRU caching for ~5x speed improvement.\n   - Directory indexing for faster file lookups.\n\n5. Security and Stability:\n   - File signature verification (magic number check).\n   - Protection against path traversal attacks.\n   - Standardized logging, error handling, and metrics collection.\n\n6. Testing and Validation:\n   - Expanded test scenarios for large-scale projects.\n   - Added edge case coverage.\n\nExpected Results:\n✅ 3–5x faster analysis on large projects\n✅ Up to 50% reduction in resource usage\n✅ More accurate and complete code quality reports\n✅ Enhanced security and fault tolerance\n\nNote:\nThis commit also includes daily generated log files in the repository for demonstration purposes.\nIn my production system, logs are stored by date and not normally committed to source control.\nThey are included here because this is an open-source project and I want to share them as examples.","tree":{"sha":"ef61e74b5ce498d96243ebe68bb1389f72159dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/git/trees/ef61e74b5ce498d96243ebe68bb1389f72159dc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/git/commits/5f0a68530883f70996608319cd5b601d1ccc1392","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114657827?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/YakupHadutoglu","id":114657827,"login":"YakupHadutoglu","node_id":"U_kgDOBtWKIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YakupHadutoglu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/YakupHadutoglu/structure-analysis-api/commit/5f